Do not try to fight enemies out of your league, which in your case seems 
it often might mean a pony.
The general advice for tough opponents apply - try to avoid the battle 
totally, let your pet do the fighting for you, choose your fighting 
ground, see that you have escape means, USE your escape means before 
dying, etc.
But when it comes to horses, cats and dogs, it is often wise to tame 
them instead of fight them. You tame these prospective pets by throwing 
them some food stuff that they like (cat/dog: tripe, meaty corpses, most 
'human food', eggs; horse: fruit, vegetables, lichen and similar 
corpses).
By taming the animal, you not only does not have to fight it, but you 
also gain a pet that can do other fighting for you. Even a pony, small 
dog or kitten is a much better fighting machine than most low level 
characters. As the pet gets more experienced by fighting, and if it gets 
properly fed, it will become an even better ally.

